## Focused producer result

Raw focused/retained result: **16/17**.

Passing evidence includes both endpoint-canonicalization contracts, typed ambiguous ring-correspondence rejection, all six previously regressed nominal G3 periodic contracts, and all seven retained G1/G2 contracts.

The sole failure is `SurfaceCellsPhase10.PeriodicPhaseFrontUsesFieldAuthoritativeAdjacentRingCorrespondence`, and it is classified **incorrect expectation / invalid witness precondition**. Production reaches `Produced`; only `exactInterRingEdges > 0` fails.

Why the witness is invalid:

- source inter-ring spacing is `0.5`;
- the test target size is `0.25`;
- production therefore uses two V-family phase-front steps per source inter-ring edge;
- no one V edge can have both endpoints at distinct exact source-ring vertices;
- the fixture remains valid; only the un-subdivided-edge witness is impossible.

The correction must observe nonzero source-attached V-family boundary-path segments reconstructed from face+barycentric provenance and assert alignment with the local authoritative V family, with a nonempty observation requirement. Do not weaken the intended field-authority assertion.

